# Interval MEC {0,1} where nature controls the long-run average via the interval.
# r(0)=4, r(1)=0. From each state: stay w.p. [0.5,1], switch w.p. [0,0.5].
#   robust (pess, nature minimises reward): nature drives the play into state 1 and keeps
#     it there (p(stay 1)=1) -> gain 0.
#   optimistic (nature maximises): nature keeps the play in state 0 (p(stay 0)=1) -> gain 4.
states 2
init 0
reward 0 4
reward 1 0
tran 0 0 0:0.5:1 1:0:0.5
tran 1 0 1:0.5:1 0:0:0.5
